---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { contactEmail } from "../lib/contact";
---

<Base
  title="Contact and comments"
  description="Contact Newton Prep about Robeson and comment on the working drafts."
>
  <article class="publication prose">
    <h1>Contact and comments</h1>
    <p>
      Newton Prep maintains Robeson. We welcome questions, corrections,
      practical experience, and proposed changes to the work published here.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    {contactEmail && (
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> for
        inquiries or comments.
      </p>
    )}
    <h2>Comment on a draft</h2>
    <p>
      Use “Comment on this draft” on a document to open an email with its title
      and address included. You can also send an email directly.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please identify the document and section, explain your concern, and
      suggest wording where useful. Include the revision date shown on the page
      if you are commenting on an earlier version.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are especially interested in whether the proposals are clear, what
      difficulties they would create in practice, and what we have overlooked.
      You do not need to review an entire document to offer a useful comment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Email comments go privately to the project team. Please tell us whether we
      may quote your comments or identify you in a published revision.
    </p>
    <h2>Contribute through GitHub</h2>
    <p>
      If you use GitHub, you can{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/robeson-org/robeson/issues">
        submit an issue
      </a>{" "}
      or propose an edit in the{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/robeson-org/robeson">repository</a>. GitHub
      contributions are public. Email and GitHub comments receive the same
      consideration.
    </p>
    <h2>Follow revisions</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/revisions/">revision history</a> records substantive
      updates. Each document links to its source history, where earlier versions
      remain available.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
